#block(width: 100%, fill: jamb-mint, stroke: 0.9pt + jamb-green, radius: 7pt, inset: 10pt)[
  #text(font: "DejaVu Sans", size: 9.2pt, weight: "bold", fill: jamb-green)[Chapter 2 in one breath]
  #v(3pt)
  #text(size: 10.1pt)[
    The novel runs on two timelines and one decision. In the present, a principal breaks down at assembly, admits five days later that he is joining his wife and children in the United Kingdom, works through a term of episodes, is given a farewell, goes to the airport on Saturday night, dreams of the slave ship at Badagry, and walks back into the school on Monday. Behind the present, twenty-four years arrive in flashbacks — Kiddies, Beesway, Fruitful Future, the prefect election and the feud. Three movements hold it: pressure in Chapters 1 to 4, the school in 5 to 8, the decision in 9 to 12. Six beats hold the present: assembly, five days, the round, farewell, Saturday, Monday. Every sequence question is answered from those beats or from the chapter that contains them — and the word *immediately* moves the answer by one place.
  ]
]

== 2.6 Chapter 2 in the Exam Hall — a Two-Minute Set

#mcq(1, [Bepo finally tells the staff that he is leaving], [at the assembly], [five days after the assembly], [after the farewell], [on the morning of his flight])

#mcq(2, [The school at which Bepo witnessed the ritual was], [Stardom Schools], [Stardom Kiddies], [Beesway Group of Schools], [Fruitful Future School])

#mcq(3, [The board caps the cooperative's loans in], [Chapter 5], [Chapter 7], [Chapter 9], [Chapter 11])

#mcq(4, [The last event narrated in the novel is], [Bepo's flight being called], [the farewell debate], [Bepo's return to the school], [the dream at the airport])

#answer-key-grid(("B", "C", "A", "C"))

#answer-notes((
  ("B", [Five days. A is the assembly, where he says nothing; C and D are later still — the farewell is Chapter 11 and the flight is Chapter 12.]),
  ("C", [Beesway, where Egi Meko was director. A and B are the same school at different levels, and D is the small school Bepo co-founded, which had no ritual but a proposition.]),
  ("A", [Chapter 5, *Snake in the Roof*. B is the ritual, C is the excursion, and D is the farewell — all real, none of them the board meeting.]),
  ("C", [The Monday return, which reverses Chapter 1. A and D are the airport on Saturday; B is Chapter 11. The novel ends at the school gate, not at the departure gate.]),
))

